                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s24IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>سورة الانبياء مكية وهي مائة واثنتاش ايوة. بِسْمِ اللّهِ الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ اقْتَرَبَ لِلنَّاسِ حِسَابُهُمْ وَهُمْ فِي غَفْلَةٍ مَّعْرِضُونَ <note>21:1</note>
                     </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#40r">-40r</locus> وَاعْتَصِمُوا بِاللَّهِ هُوَ مَوْلَاكُمْ فَنِعْمَ الْمَوْلَى وَنِعْمَ النَّصِيرُ <note>22:78</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>21:1-22:78. Some words are divided into two different lines.
The “ḏāl” is written with the dot inside. Sometimes the catchword is only the first part of the first word in the next page, sometimes there is a repeated word and the catchword is the second word of the next page. 
The name of the scribe appears in mss. 4521D (37r) and 4521X (1v, 45v). The note stating that he is actually the scribe is in 4521X (45v).  </note>
                     <note/>
